 "prose": [
  {
   "tag": "a",
   "id": null,
   "text": "← Unfold"
  },
  {
   "tag": "h1",
   "id": null,
   "text": "Homotopy explorer"
  },
  {
   "tag": "label",
   "id": null,
   "text": "Category"
  },
  {
   "tag": "select",
   "id": "choose-category",
   "text": "HomotopiesCan / cannotHomotopy classes (maps)Homotopy types (spaces)"
  },
  {
   "tag": "label",
   "id": null,
   "text": "Example"
  },
  {
   "tag": "select",
   "id": "choose-example",
   "text": "Circle: open the loop? — failsAnnulus: go around the hole? — failsAnnulus: straight to a point — failsAnnulus → its inner circle — worksAround the hole once → twice — impossibleA loop beside the hole → a point — worksCircle → circle: straight shrink — fails"
  },
  {
   "tag": "button",
   "id": null,
   "text": "▶ Play"
  },
  {
   "tag": "output",
   "id": null,
   "text": "0.50"
  },
  {
   "tag": "button",
   "id": "homotopy-connections",
   "text": "Connect points"
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "id": null,
   "text": "Every point stays in Y, but the marked neighbors split at a seam. This is not continuous."
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "id": null,
   "text": "X = annulus"
  },
  {
   "tag": "h2",
   "id": null,
   "text": "Input x"
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "id": null,
   "text": "Y = same annulus"
  },
  {
   "tag": "h2",
   "id": null,
   "text": "Start f₀(x)"
  },
  {
   "tag": "h2",
   "id": null,
   "text": "Attempt fₜ(x)"
  },
  {
   "tag": "h2",
   "id": null,
   "text": "End f₁(x)"
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "id": null,
   "text": "Same color = same input. Click or drag on a colored shape to circle corresponding points."
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "id": null,
   "text": "The outputs stay in Y, but the map jumps across the seam between a and b."
  },
  {
   "tag": "span",
   "id": null,
   "text": "The hatched hole is not part of Y."
  },
  {
   "tag": "summary",
   "id": null,
   "text": "Why?"
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "id": null,
   "text": "Each point can travel around the hole to the destination. The problem is choosing all these paths continuously together."
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "id": null,
   "text": "Look at points of radius ¾ approaching the right-hand seam from above and below. At t = ½, their outputs approach (¾,0) and (−¾,0), even though their inputs approach the same point. The halfway map is discontinuous."
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "id": null,
   "text": "This rules out this attempt. The general obstruction is winding: a loop going once around the hole cannot become a constant loop while remaining in the annulus."
  },
  {
   "tag": "p",
   "id": null,
   "text": "Background: Winding number (Hatcher, §1.1)."
  },
  {
   "tag": "a",
   "id": null,
   "text": "Background: Winding number (Hatcher, §1.1)."
  }
